payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3a20428469cc3a16e72238797ff6adc86b79958234b17a191aeed1bac96f64dc","event_uuid":"43e99d4c-748e-4205-8d0d-7eeceb15e0d7","position":{"commit_sha":"c199efd6fee330f742dcc4d31de40777dd6d2c2d","position":"1785189219638550838-43e99d4c-748e-4205-8d0d-7eeceb15e0d7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5ad00e7b19e2946d67ac1356f711d27af2b9cd609c1ff9ef94d95d98f69be435","event_uuid":"ce951d18-90b7-4515-a920-5b4fdd6eaa06","position":{"commit_sha":"ae61b29cb7259aa0f887259d833106a0aa7d3508","position":"1785189498941357001-ce951d18-90b7-4515-a920-5b4fdd6eaa06"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1e43cfca4671f8fd6f304522e7cad1720eb6bde31ffa6e8e2100c95c408e779e","event_uuid":"42644f73-90a4-4a32-9e84-7113cb9e3b19","position":{"commit_sha":"d4ad60c568e6c4ec8f9138781e0325dc4c76bb2e","position":"1785189581640693001-42644f73-90a4-4a32-9e84-7113cb9e3b19"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"622ce86f77c9bd24d4ce6ab60eda73ee7f6ce8df84a462d5d63456358c2c2216","event_uuid":"fae85472-670b-442f-ab34-373944225330","position":{"commit_sha":"c60b1105a49000cd6be870a3a1afa884fe1756e0","position":"1785189584438140001-fae85472-670b-442f-ab34-373944225330"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Analysis complete against origin/main bc838aed2.\n\nCurrent measure\n- `_clarity_score` awards generic points for any H2 heading, >=200 chars, >=500 chars, and any dash bullet, then type-specific bonuses. `clarity_check_compute` separately requires >=1 AC checkbox. The DET P1 copy records the same score as coverage but does not block on it.\n- This rewards volume and legacy per-type shape, not the author guide leaf/container contract. A padded ticket can pass with no Approach, grounded Scope, or per-criterion verification.\n- The score is duplicated in `_engine_support/gates.py` and `llm/plan_review/det_floor.py`; the latter already lacks the bug branch, so extending two copies invites drift.\n\nRecommended deterministic additions, in priority order\n1. Required-section shape keyed on graph altitude, not ticket type. Parse sections once. All plans: nonempty Context/Problem and AC. Leaf: nonempty Approach and Scope. Container: AC plus graph-backed child decomposition. Do not require Testing deterministically because applicability depends on whether behavior is testable. A heading counts only if it has nonblank content before the next H2.\n2. Per-AC verification coverage. Parse wrapped checkbox items; each must either start `[operator-attested]` or contain an explicit proving/check clause (`verified by`, `verify with`, `checked by`) with a command, test, CI check, or concrete artifact assertion. Report proved_items / total_items and treat incomplete coverage as advisory until corpus evaluation demonstrates precision.\n3. Placeholder-free executable scope. Case-insensitive exact detection of the guide lexicon in Scope/Approach bullets: TBD, figure out, verify whether, check if, depends on investigation, choose an appropriate X. Ignore fenced/code/quoted examples. Any hit should cap or penalize clarity because it explicitly defers a decision.\n4. Grounded edit-set. For leaves, require a nonempty Scope plus structured file_impact, rather than the current path-like slash regex. The graph/state-aware scorer can use the canonical file-impact field. Existence and consumer completeness remain G1G2/LLM judgments because new paths are valid.\n5. AC text hygiene, reusing P6 at the AC-item level: flag bundled independent outcomes, subjective terms, exact `works correctly`, and unproved hedges (`should`, `probably`, `seems`). Avoid whole-plan vague-word scanning; numeric thresholds or explicit proof clauses should suppress obvious false positives.\n6. Testing shape when Testing is declared: require one happy-path marker and one failure/edge/empty/invalid/timeout/boundary marker. If cutover/default/migration language is present, advise a live/end-to-end proving marker. Do not infer Testing applicability deterministically.\n7. Nonempty Context/Problem and Approach sections are safe structural signals. Persona/problem quality, mechanism correctness, positive-rationale quality, alternatives, coherence, child coverage, and whether a test truly exercises the change must remain LLM-reviewed.\n\nScoring recommendation\n- Replace raw length and any-bullet points with named applicable checks and return per-check evidence. Derive the compatibility score from satisfied/applicable checks; do not simply add more points to the current seven-point scale, since filler would still compensate for a missing required section.\n\nDocumentation conflicts\n- Current author/user guides still request Success Criteria for containers/epics, but the heading is inert in tests and active epic 1386 / docs child 44c7 own its collapse into Acceptance Criteria. Do not encode Success Criteria.\n- The author guide requires naming a rejected alternative, while authoritative G6 says require positive rationale and explicitly do not require rejected-alternative prose. No open ticket covered that conflict, so bug 828a-7407-9d68-4b82 was created and linked discovered_from this task. Until fixed, clarity should check only nonempty Approach, not rejected-alternative wording.\n\nEvidence: src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md:49-87, src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py:108-140, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py:154-233 and P6, docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md:E2/E5/E6/F1/G1G2/G6, tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py:5-13.","timestamp":1785189113645535001}],"created_at":1785188370445925001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nCompare rebar's author-facing guidance for writing a passing plan with the deterministic criteria currently contributing to the clarity measure. Identify meaningful, mechanically testable additions without changing code.\n\n## Plan\n- Read the packaged plan-writing guide and relevant plan-review criteria documentation.\n- Locate the current clarity measure and enumerate its deterministic inputs.\n- Map documented guidance to candidate checks, filtering out semantic judgments that cannot be reliably deterministic.\n- Recommend prioritized criteria, including detection rules, likely failure modes, and false-positive controls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Current clarity checks and documented plan-writing guidance are compared using repository citations.\n- [ ] Each recommended criterion has a deterministic detection rule and rationale.\n- [ ] Recommendations distinguish strong additions from checks that should remain LLM-reviewed.\n- [ ] Findings are recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"42644f73-90a4-4a32-9e84-7113cb9e3b19","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["analysis","plan-review","clarity"],"ticket_id":"02d3-1b66-f194-48b6","ticket_type":"task","title":"Assess deterministic clarity criteria against plan-writing guidance","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b8172af0-e589-485e-850b-2316ea19a66b","05e5f740-2bb9-42db-87a6-6b7177fa1164","3c1a82b5-4294-4e19-981e-d2a9060993f6","e5a82891-63b7-4751-9410-b9696c2387ea","da36b68f-d71a-470a-ae04-2231be649857","68b461de-4774-40d0-83cf-4788a96587d1","5815d3f7-dbd3-4551-a7b3-b64689fa3efb","43e99d4c-748e-4205-8d0d-7eeceb15e0d7","ce951d18-90b7-4515-a920-5b4fdd6eaa06","42644f73-90a4-4a32-9e84-7113cb9e3b19","fae85472-670b-442f-ab34-373944225330"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786666591064015799,"uuid":"39c162b9-aba7-4573-b131-eb70231beed7"}